## External evidence mapped to local P0 and guardrails

| External evidence | Local mapping | Audit consequence for v18 |
|---|---|---|
| Buffer channel selection, previews, scheduling choices, draft recovery, separate scheduled-post edits | D02, E01, E06, E09, P0 canonical lineage | Preserve per-platform customization and recoverable drafts. Do not use a bulk-success shell that erases channel-specific revisions or results. |
| Sprout role/profile approval, multi-step approvers, expiry, rejection, revision and resubmission | A05, C06, E03, E04, E11, P0 customer approval | Campaign brief and artifact approval must show actor, role, target profile, content/time binding, expiry, change history, rejection reason, and safe resubmission. |
| Jasper Knowledge Base and Brand Voice create, preview, save, apply and default behavior | B01 to B17, P0 knowledge and tone lifecycle | v18 needs a visible source-to-guide/tone workflow and applied-context inspector. OSMU adds immutable versions and customer approval because an agency/client boundary is stricter than a personal writing tool. |
| NN/g progressive-disclosure evidence | H01, D09, E03, P0 truthful decision surface | Identity, readiness, rights, approval and publish consequences stay visible at the decision point. Only secondary diagnostics may collapse. |
| Scheibehenne et al. (2010) heterogeneous choice-overload result | H04, D01, D05 | Categorize and provide novice recommendations plus expert shortcuts. Do not delete valid platforms or tools under a blanket “less choice” claim. |
| Johnson and Goldstein (2003) default effects | H03, E05, D06 | External publish and Messaging default OFF. Enabling requires named account, scope, approval consequence and reversible consent. |
| Nunes and Drèze (2006) endowed-progress effect | H02, A01 to A03, D11 | Setup progress advances only from persisted server evidence. A callback, route visit, pasted credential or local draft cannot earn a completed step. |

