#### Normative secret-class matrix

| Secret class | Raw visibility contract | Current code and historical truth | v18 required state | Test evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Customer channel OAuth access/refresh token | Raw DOM/network/log/export/reveal `0`, including Admin default screens. | `lib/channel-accounts.ts` stores `secret_enc` and `refresh_enc`; `app/api/channels/[provider]/accounts/route.ts` returns the `listChannelAccounts` whitelist; AccountManager consumes identity/status metadata. | Settings exposes only exact account identity, scopes, expiry, health, verified/readiness state and reconnect/revoke. No reveal action exists. | Seed access and refresh canaries; scan customer, Admin support, account APIs, browser history, telemetry, errors and exports for exact/prefix matches `0`; reconnect rotates server-side credentials without readback. |
| Tenant automation API token | Plaintext exactly once in the successful issue response/screen; server stores hash plus non-secret metadata; every later list is masked with reveal `0`. | `lib/tenant-auth.ts::issueTenantToken` returns the new raw token while inserting only `token_hash`; `app/api/tenant-tokens/route.ts` lists metadata and revokes; `components/settings/TenantTokensSettings.tsx` says “지금만 표시” and holds the issue response in transient state. | One-time copy screen, explicit acknowledgement/close, label/created/last-used/status list, rotate and revoke. Rotation issues a new token before revoking the selected old token; it never re-reveals the old value. | Assert successful issue response plaintext count `1`, DB raw0/hash1, reload/list/reveal raw0, rotate produces different token, revoke makes old token 401, and tenant B use is denied. |
| Operator OAuth app Client Secret | Timed raw reveal is allowed only after exact operator reauth and explicit reveal intent/reason, from encrypted DB source only. | `app/api/operator/oauth-credentials/route.ts`, `lib/oauth-app-credentials.ts`, and Admin UI already provide operator bearer auth, pgcrypto DB storage, env import, `no-store`, mask and 30-second clear. Session-state records live DB-source reveal without logging the value. Reauth and actor/reason audit are not implemented. | Env HTTP reveal `0`; complete env set imports to encrypted DB first. A fresh exact operator reauth then explicit reveal confirmation/reason enables DB-source response only, `no-store`, 30-second auto-clear, manual hide, and actor/reason/time audit. Customer/cross-tenant `0`. | Route matrix plus reauth TTL, explicit-intent, env-direct-deny, import conflict, DB reveal, 30-second DOM clear and audit tests; canary absent from logs/errors/audit/storage snapshots other than the encrypted DB field and transient no-store response. |
| BYOK/customer-supplied secret | Write-only input, masked/configured state afterward, raw reveal `0`. | `app/api/integrations/route.ts` encrypts `secret_enc` and GET returns `has_secret`; `components/settings/AiKeySettings.tsx` clears the input after save and displays configured/billing state. | Password/write-only replacement field, validation health, billing owner, updated time, rotate/replace and revoke; never prefill or reveal stored value. | Save canary, reload and inspect DOM/network/log/error/analytics/export for raw/prefix `0`; replacement invalidates old key use; tenant B cannot see configured metadata or mutate it. |

### H. Psychology guardrails: reject persuasive UX that weakens truth

| ID / basis | Atomic guardrail | Existing implementation and code/wiki path | v17 | v18 required screen or state | Required test evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| H01 · readiness/truth doctrine | Progressive disclosure must not hide account identity, readiness, approval, rights, or publish consequences. | `P` current account/status detail is distributed and sometimes ambiguous. | `P` Header7 is strong, but compact/mobile layouts may conceal consequential context. | Keep identity + readiness + target + approval consequence in the decision surface; only secondary diagnostics may collapse. | At 390/1024/1440, publish/approve decision can be made without opening hidden help; exact blocker remains visible. |
| H02 · honest progress | Endowed progress must never mark setup steps complete from mere route visit, callback, or local draft. | `P` historical OAuth false-success makes this a live risk. | `N/P` readiness ladder exists; onboarding progress is not explicit. | Progress step completes only on server-read evidence; partial progress names remaining condition; no celebratory completion early. | Fault each onboarding/readiness step; completed count never advances without persisted verified state. |
| H03 · safe defaults / L-34 | Defaults may bias users, so external publish and community messaging default OFF with explicit account and approval consequence. | `P` settings/policies exist, but fresh-tenant default needs direct proof. | `Y/P` Messaging OFF and approval variants are visible. | Default OFF, explicit opt-in, named account/scope, reversible setting, audit event. | Fresh tenant/state reset: zero external calls until opt-in; toggle change requires consequence confirmation. |
| H04 · choice overload evidence | Do not claim “fewer options is always better”; choice-overload effects are heterogeneous and context-dependent. | `P` current surfaces have many choices without consistent categorization. | `P` three rails/categories help; expert acceleration is incomplete. | Categorize by job (text → card-news → video; Social → Messaging), recommend contextually, and provide search/recent/template or expert jump. | Novice path reaches a valid first draft; expert can jump directly; no options deleted solely under a blanket psychology claim. |

## v18 hard blockers and non-blocking preservation

### P0: design cannot be called complete without these

1. **Knowledge Center state set** inside an existing approved surface or overlay: import existing wiki, create new wiki, edit, sync, diff/history, last-good failure recovery.
2. **Brand Guide + Tone state set**: generate draft, edit, immutable version, human approval, active version, artifact-level application proof.
3. **Campaign Brief state set**: goal, audience, offer/CTA, budget disposition (`No paid spend` is valid and safest default), deadline/timezone, brand safety, claims, asset-rights readiness, customer approval/version.
4. **Cross-surface canonical lineage**: same campaign/artifact revision through Studio, Inbox/Queue, Calendar, Videos, channel owner, result/permalink, analytics, learning.
5. **Feedback application proof**: performance evidence ID and exactly one approved change appear in the next generation input and revision diff.
6. **Mobile usability retake**: fixed bulk actions may not cover the card being reviewed; overlap evidence is required, not only horizontal-overflow math.
7. **Truthful defaults and progress**: publish/messaging OFF until explicit account/scope/approval; no fake completed onboarding/readiness step.
8. **Two distinct orders**: sidebar is `Social → Messaging → Social video`; Studio production is `Text → Photo/Card-news → Video`. One order must never be inferred from or substituted for the other.

### Preserve from v17

- familiar current shell and route25/destination26 ownership;
- exact sidebar sequence `Social → Messaging → Social video`, with Messaging default OFF;
- exact Studio sequence `Text → Photo/Card-news → Video`, with per-card edit, bulk selection, and direct-vs-approval policy;
- Header7 and account switch/reconnect model;
- detailed video workbench and video rights states;
- aggregate whitelist separated from native provider metrics;
- customer/operator shells, Settings8/Settings9, Admin cannot publish for customer;
- same customer-language title/revision across surfaces, but replace fixture-only continuity with inspectable IDs.

## Self-question and revision

### “이 체크리스트가 틀렸다면 왜?”

1. It could over-expand a focused content publishing product into an agency CRM, paid-ad manager, or full wiki CMS.
2. It could mistake a clickable prototype for an implementation and demand network behavior from the design stage.
3. It could reward visible completeness by putting every truth field on every screen, creating cognitive overload.
4. It could treat a width/overflow assertion as responsive success while a fixed control still covers the work.
5. It could preserve the appealing “next draft” loop while failing to prove the performance signal actually changed generation.

**steelman 반론:** v17 already contains 26 destinations, Header7, three Studio rails, approval states, video rights, analytics separation and a next-draft CTA. Adding wiki CRUD, guide/tone versioning and a campaign brief could make a two-week content product feel like an agency ERP, so a reasonable designer would keep those concepts behind one compact Knowledge and Campaign drawer rather than create more top-level routes. The audit accepts that interface compression, but it does not accept removing the underlying version, approval and application states.

**premortem:** three months after v18 approval, a customer publishes an outdated price from a silently overwritten guide, then cannot tell which account, approval, rights record or performance suggestion produced the post. The prototype had looked complete because the same title was repeated across screens, but no canonical ID or immutable version existed. This failure is prevented only if the semantic test follows one seeded campaign and exact revision through source, brief, guide/tone, artifact, approval, job, permalink, metric and next input.

**kill-criteria:** reject the v18 design retake if any P0 set lacks a visible screen/state and semantic acceptance path, if any of L-01 to L-45 has zero atomic row, if sidebar order differs from Social → Messaging → Social video, if Studio order differs from Text → Photo/Card-news → Video, or if the 390 px test reports overlap/occlusion above zero. Reject any “feedback loop complete” claim when the next artifact lacks the source result ID and exact approved changed variable.

### Revision applied after the challenge

- Campaign budget is narrowed to **budget disposition/cap and explicit no-paid-spend**, not ad buying, bidding, billing, or autonomous spend.
- New-wiki scope is narrowed to the minimum evidence store needed for brand facts: create/edit/version/sync/approve; it need not become a general-purpose document suite.
- Design gates require screen/state/semantic click evidence; live adapter, OAuth, permalink, and native metric claims remain separately `U` until build/QA production-parity evidence exists.
- Consequential truth stays at the decision point; diagnostics can progressively disclose. Categorization and expert shortcuts are preferred over deleting options under a universal “choice overload” claim.
- Responsive acceptance includes occlusion and operability, not just `scrollWidth`.
- “Apply next insight” passes only when the next artifact exposes evidence/result IDs, the approved changed variable, and a before/after diff.

## Planning standard seven-principle audit

| Principle | PASS/FAIL | Evidence in this audit |
|---|---|---|
| Terminology consistency | PASS | Status legend fixes `E/P/M/U` and v17 `Y/P/N`; canonical campaign/artifact/job/result/learning vocabulary is repeated across rows. |
| Concrete limits | PASS | 96 atomic rows before research retake, route25/destination26, Header7, Settings8/Settings9, 1440/1024/390 and platform-by-platform rows are explicit. |
| Input/output separation | PASS | Every atomic row separates current input truth, required v18 state, and observable test evidence. |
| Cross-feature consistency | PASS | D05 and P0 separate sidebar order from Studio production order; E09 and F07 test shared identity and next-input propagation. |
| Policy detail | PASS | Defaults, approval invalidation, rights, uncertainty, partial results, retry, secret redaction and role boundaries include edge behavior. |
| Extraction completeness | PASS | L-01 to L-45 coverage script reports missing 0; required agency and psychology omissions have dedicated rows. |
| Logical/testable wording | PASS | Each row has a falsifiable acceptance observation instead of “intuitive,” “easy,” or route-click-only completion language. |

## Final conclusion

**v17 is a strong publishing-control prototype but an incomplete marketing-agency operating loop.** Its most important remaining omission is not another route or prettier card: it is the missing, inspectable chain from customer-owned knowledge and an approved campaign brief through approved brand/tone versions, rights and safety review, canonical execution, provider proof, and one evidence-backed change applied to the next generation. v18 should close those semantic contracts while preserving the good account/publish/analytics work already present.

